# PART 4: BUILD A CENTRAL ACADEMIC PERFORMANCE & GRADING ENGINE

This is the central feature of the project.

The application must be able to calculate a learner's overall academic performance for a defined reporting period.

The calculation should use all eligible and properly graded academic records associated with the learner during that period.

The system must support:

- Assessments.
- Quizzes.
- Assignments.
- Projects.
- Class activities.
- Tests.
- Examinations.
- Practical tasks.
- Other explicitly scored academic work.

The system must also incorporate qualitative academic evidence from:

- Attendance.
- Learning milestones.
- Programme progression.
- Completed practical achievements.
- Tutor feedback.
- General learner participation.

However, do not automatically convert ungraded milestones or attendance statuses into academic scores.

Numerical performance and qualitative learner development must remain distinguishable.

