# PART 7: ACADEMIC PERIOD AND CALENDAR MANAGEMENT

The reporting engine needs genuine academic periods.

Do not rely on manually typed academic-session text as the only way to determine which assessments belong in a particular report.

The existing `academicSession` field in the document-header configuration is descriptive metadata, not a complete academic calendar.

Create or extend an appropriate Academic Period Management system.

## 1. School academic sessions

Support school-specific academic sessions.

Each academic session must contain:

- Session name.
- School ID.
- Start date.
- End date.
- Session status.
- Term 1.
- Term 2.
- Term 3.

Each term must have:

- Term name.
- Start date.
- End date.
- Reporting status.
- Optional reporting notes.

Example:

2026/2027 Academic Session

- Term 1: Exact configured dates.
- Term 2: Exact configured dates.
- Term 3: Exact configured dates.

The dates must be configured by an authorized platform administrator or tutor assigned to that school.

Do not guess term dates.

## 2. Private learner programme periods

Private learners require programme-based reporting periods.

Resolve the actual enrolment and programme association.

Where available, use:

- Programme ID.
- Programme name.
- Programme start date.
- Programme completion date.
- Module progression.
- Programme status.
- Assigned tutor.

The end-of-programme report should be tied to the actual learner's selected programme.

Where dates are missing, allow an authorized user to configure the reporting period explicitly.

Do not assume that every private programme lasts one year.

## 3. Private learner annual period

Support an independently defined one-year reporting period.

The tutor or administrator must be able to select the precise start and end dates.

The period should support a clear annual academic summary, even where the learner is enrolled in multiple programmes.

## 4. Period membership

An academic item must belong to a reporting period based on its actual relevant completion or submission date.

Examples:

- An examination belongs to the period in which the learner submitted the attempt.
- An assignment belongs to the period in which the learner completed the eligible submission.
- An attendance record belongs to the actual class date.
- A completed milestone belongs to its completion date.

Do not assign work to a term merely because its creation date or due date falls within that term.

Where source records lack reliable dates, flag them for review.

